{"title":"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many integers greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, written in base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> notation, are increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when their digits are reversed?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e4baf656542552e2f6fb67cda4954997184a2ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 1 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 8 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 9 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"357\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let our two digit number be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/8/e980eec360016ff6469164708ab65aef5fe83181.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{ab}$\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the tens digit, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is the ones digit. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/e/a5e8d95dc7748dd5c11312c321785208f430ae21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{ab}=10a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />. When we reverse our digits, it becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/91637b4521e1c07f0aa214e1070b7c2f81c10967.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10b+a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f69a26da4f2b57e1559aa2c759646ac0716e325.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10a+b+9=10b+a\\implies a-b=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"292\" height=\"14\" />. So, our numbers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/b/45bb0f530790de109ef905a4cbeaa82108eb6e48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12, 23, 34, 45, 56, 67, 78, 89\\Rightarrow \\textbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"258\" height=\"17\" />.~MathJams\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME\" title=\"1976 AHSME\">1976 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1976 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1976\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME\" title=\"1975 AHSME\">1975 AHSME</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_AHSME\" title=\"1977 AHSME\">1977 AHSME</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1976 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_AHSME_P